      "fragment_index": 3,
      "start": 114.15,
      "end": 179.2,
      "duration": 65.05,
      "text": "Alongside these pillars, the Foundation also supports core capabilities of the core. Most notably, the ongoing development and delivery of a Christchurch Response Protocol, seeking to de-escalate after violence. The rise of new AI tools has transformed our technology landscape, bringing enormous potential, but also significant responsibility. AI can relieve the burdens of repetitive tasks, unlock creativity, a powerful shift. But we must also recognise that AI remains poorly understood by many, and that's where risks emerge. Synthetic content, especially when used to inflame divisions or distort reality as a growing concern. And yet, if harnessed responsibility frontier models and emerging tech, strengthen trust and safety tools and help protect people more effectively than ever before. The Christchurch call is committed to ensuring that AI systems, especially those used for content moderation and recommendation algorithms, are developed and deployed with safety, security and ethics at their core.",
