      "fragment_index": 5,
      "start": 239.06,
      "end": 297.56,
      "duration": 58.5,
      "text": "For safe guards to prevent AI misuse and spreading violent extremist content, for continued research into algorithmic amplification and its effects on users. For exploration of adversarial attacks and AI system resilience, for alignment with international efforts to ensure that radicalisation and violent extremism remains central to global AI governance. And above all, for ongoing dialogue across governments, tech companies, civil society and academia, focused on the intersection of new technologies and our specialist domain area. The Christchurch call believes the future of digital safety, especially around terrorist and violent extremist content, hinges on how we govern AI today right now. As AI increasingly shapes online spaces, the risks of misuse, whether through violent extremist content, algorithmic bias or opaque decision-making, require urgent coordinated action.",
